nking about  gentrification were you thinking about  becoming a parent what was the genesis  of the idea and is the idea then start  finding a location and a story as you  say I have two kids 24 year old twins  and and so I'm a I'm a  parent i'm also a son and i think I'm 50  so I'm sort of in some very middle point  and and I'm often thinking about my role  as both a new generation of parent and  also what my responsibilities and what  I've learned from in terms of my own  father and that relationship I'm  interested in these generational crosses  and I think this film is really it's  about these two kids but it's also  deeply about the parents generation as  well and the marriage and and and being  a mother and all these different things  so I I wanted to make a film that  focused on childhood in its relationship  to adult life and I also wanted to make  a kind of film that I'm really miss  which is a sort of cinematic film that  has childhood maybe at its center but  that is not animated and it's not a  superhero film and it's a kind of film  like the world of in orient or or like a  movie like cast by Ken Loach or the 400  blows or the red balloon all these  movies that introduced for me as a young  person some of the beauties of  moviemaking and and I wanted to try to  capture that innocence from your very  first movie that delta which is largely  autobiographical a lot of your own life  is reflected in your movies but you also  work with a co-writer so how do you  balance what you feel and what you  understand with somebody who may not  feel or understand or share those  experiences you know it's like it's it's  a collaboration and a relationship and  and and when it works it can be very  beautiful Mauricio Zacharias is from he  lives we both lived in New York for  about 20 years he's from Rio we tend to  bring in bits and pieces of our lives  we're also now a form of family he's the  Godfather of my son you know we are a  communal family in a way when we star